  "theorem_contract": {
    "young_branching_reciprocity": "sum_{alpha in nu^-} d_alpha = d_nu for every parent nu |- n, and sum_{nu : alpha in nu^-} d_nu = n * d_alpha for every child alpha |- n-1, proving exact multiplicity conservation.",
    "computational_basis_diagonal_invariance": "For every left-covariant point POVM M_j = L(x_j) (T_H / n) L(x_j)^dagger, [M_j]_{g, g} == 1/n! identically for all g in S_n and all j in {0, ..., n-1}, forcing p(j | tau) == 1/n on diagonal mixed coset states with I(tau(n) : J) == 0.0 bits identically.",
    "peter_weyl_conclusive_probability_identity": "The sum of raw measurement overlaps across all n outcomes satisfies sum_{j=0}^{n-1} raw_overlap(j) == p(n) / n! identically. The conclusive measurement probability collapses as P_concl = p(n) / n! = 2^{-Omega(n log n)}.",
    "physical_bias_and_mutual_information_extinction": "The physical bias on legal normalized POVMs is bounded by Delta_phys <= p(n) / n! = 2^{-Omega(n log n)}. Single-copy mutual information collapses as I(tau(n) : J) <= (2/ln 2) n (p(n)/n!)^2 = 2^{-Omega(n log n)} bits. Copy complexity to distinguish tau(n) requires N_copies >= (n! / p(n))^2 = 2^{Omega(n log n)}.",
    "class_algebra_commutant_invariance": "All central / class-algebra POVM effects commute with S_n, giving identical outcome distributions p(lambda | tau) across each conjugacy class C = ct(tau) with I(tau | ct(tau) : Lambda) == 0.0 bits. Total recovered entropy is at most log_2 p(n) = O(sqrt{n}) bits, leaving Theta(n log n) bits unrecovered.",
    "universal_trilemma_barrier": "Every uniform harmonic Naimark dilation faces an exhaustive trilemma between central zero-information, point-stabilizer factorial purity decay, and uncompressed exponential dilation dimension."
  },
